// TWO cross-namespace visibility rejections, in ONE build.
//
//   1. `m1::PRIV` — a namespace-qualified VALUE reference to a `private` module-level const
//      declared in another namespace (#594 crumb 8c / issue #613).
//   2. `leaksub::leak()` — a `private` member const read through an inheriting subclass declared
//      in ANOTHER namespace (#594 crumb 7 bounce fix). It moved here from the
//      `member_const_visibility_leak_rejected` project, which is now the PARSE-stage fold host and
//      therefore can no longer reach the checker at all (see this project's `.tkr` header).
//
// Both must be REJECTED, and both diagnostics must appear in this ONE build.
exit((m1::PRIV + leaksub::leak()) to i32)
